uirements and Evaluation (SQuaRE) — Data quality model (https://www.iso.org/standard/35736.html)\nciteturn54view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn53view6\",\"lineno\":40}); Total lines: 183\nL0: cite0†Image L1: \nL2: Reference number\nL3: ISO/IEC 25012:2008\nL4: \nL5: © ISO 2026\nL6: \nL7: International Standard\nL8: \nL9: ISO/IEC 25012:2008\nL10: \nL11: Software engineering — Software product Quality Requirements and Evaluation (SQuaRE) — Data quality model\nL12: \nL13: Edition 1\nL14: 2008-12\nL15: \nL16: Preview this standard in our Online Browsing Platform (OBP)\nL17: \nL18: [Button: Read sample]\nL19: \nL20: cite1†Published (Edition 1, 2008)\nL21: \nL22: This publication was last reviewed and confirmed in 2025. Therefore this version remains current.\nL23: ### ISO/IEC 25012:2008\nL24: \nL25: Language\nL26: \nL27: [Select]\nL28: \nL29: Format\nL30: \nL31: [Input] PDF\nL32: \nL33: [Input] Paper\nL34: \nL35: CHF (Swiss francs) 100\nL36: \nL37: [Button: Add to cart]\nL38: \nL39: Convert Swiss francs (CHF) to cite2†your currency†www.xe.com L40: \nL41: ### Preview ISO/IEC 25012:2008\nL42: ## Abstract\nL43: \nL44: ISO/IEC 25012:2008 defines a general data quality model for data retained in a structured format within a computer system.\nL45: \nL46: ISO/IEC 25012:2008 can be used to establish data quality requirements, define data quality measures, or plan and perform data quality evaluations. It could be used, for example,\nL47:   * to define and evaluate data quality requirements in data production, acquisition and integration processes,\nL48:   * to identify data quality assurance criteria, also useful for re-engineering, assessment and improvement of data,\nL49:   * to evaluate the compliance of data with legislation and/or requirements.\nL50: ISO/IEC 25012:2008 categorizes quality attributes into fifteen characteristics considered by two points of view: inherent and system dependent. Data quality characteristics will be of varying importance and priority to different stakeholders.\nL51: \nL52: ISO/IEC 25012:2008 is intended to be used in conjunction with the other parts of the SQuaRE series of International Standards, and with ISO/IEC 9126-1 until superseded by ISO/IEC 25010.\nL53: ## General information\nL54: \nL55:   * Status\nL56: \nL57:  : Published\nL58: \nL59: Publication date\nL60: \nL61:  : 2008-12\nL62: \nL63: Stage\nL64: \nL65: : International Standard confirmed [cite1†90.93 ]\nL66: \nL67:   * Edition\nL68: \nL69:  : 1\nL70: \nL71: Number of pages\nL72: \nL73:  : 13\nL74: \nL75:   * Technical Committee :\nL76: \nL77: cite3†ISO/IEC JTC 1/SC 7 L78: \nL79: ICS :\nL80: \nL81: cite4†35.080 L82: \nL83:   * cite5†RSS updates\nL84: \nL85: ## Life cycle\nL86: \nL87:   * ### Now\nL88: \nL89: Published\nL90: #### ISO/IEC 25012:2008\nL91: \nL92: A standard is reviewed every 5 years\nL93: cite6†Stage: 90.93 (Confirmed) L94: \nL95:     * 00\nL96: \nL97: Preliminary\nL98: \nL99:     * 10\nL100: \nL101: Proposal\nL102: \nL103:       * cite7†10.99 2004-10-22 New project approved L104:     * 20\nL105: \nL106: Preparatory\nL107: \nL108:       * cite8†20.00 2005-07-08 New project registered in TC/SC work programme L109:       * cite9†20.20 2005-07-08 Working draft (WD) study initiated L110:       * cite10†20.99 2005-10-13 WD approved for registration as CD L111:     * 30\nL112: \nL113: Committee\nL114:       * cite11†30.00 2005-10-13 Committee draft (CD) registered L115:       * cite12†30.20 2006-02-05 CD consultation initiated L116:       * cite13†30.60 2006-06-30 Close of comment period L117:       * cite14†30.99 2007-01-28 CD approved for registration as DIS L118:     * 40\nL119: \nL120: Enquiry\nL121:       * cite15†40.00 2007-01-28 DIS registered L122:       * cite16†40.20 2007-06-29 DIS ballot initiated: 12 weeks L123:       * cite17†40.60 2007-10-30 Close of voting L124:       * cite18†40.93 2008-01-02 Full report